# COMPONENT

## KnowledgeWorkbench

### STYLE

full-fledged-with-standalone

### PACKAGE

org.simplemodeling.textus.knowledgeworkbench

### DESCRIPTION

Forms Information Candidates for human work. Supports starter registration/search
and provider-neutral proposal registration with durable source-key lookup. Sequential
resend returns the current candidate without overwriting edits or original proposal
metadata. Uses a stable standalone identity and the CNCF native persistent datastore.
Human formation and explicit review decisions retain the exact evidence target.
Human-facing Workbench views expose available evidence and its limitations.
KnowledgeHub Admission remains separate Phase 1.1 work.

### COMPONENTLET

#### public-candidate

#### candidate-admin

# COMPONENTLET

## public-candidate

- component :: KnowledgeWorkbench
- kind :: participant

### DESCRIPTION

Declares the participant intended for public Candidate registration and search.
The current factory constructs only the primary participant; this declaration
does not enable MCP publication.

# COMPONENTLET

## candidate-admin

- component :: KnowledgeWorkbench
- kind :: participant

### DESCRIPTION

Declares the participant intended for administrative Candidate work. The current
factory does not instantiate this participant or publish its services through MCP.

# SERVICE

## Candidate

### DESCRIPTION

Registers and searches Information Candidates and source proposals for the current user.
Operations require a stable user identity and the native persistent application
datastore supplied by the CNCF Subsystem.

### OPERATION

#### registerCandidate

##### DESCRIPTION

Creates a native InformationCandidate using a required name and optional
description. This command persists a new entity and returns its native id and name.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterCandidate

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterCandidateResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-create

##### ENTITY
InformationCandidate

#### registerProposal

##### DESCRIPTION

Validates one proposal JSON object and searches its exact producerRef/proposalId key.
Creates a native candidate when absent; sequential resend returns the current
candidate with created=false without any incoming-field write. Retains the exact
first originalProposal and supplied evidence/material/source references.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterProposal

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterProposalResult

#### findCandidateByProposal

##### DESCRIPTION

Finds the current accessible candidate by exact, case-sensitive producerRef and
proposalId. Returns an optional candidate without writes. Ambiguous visible
correspondence fails explicitly instead of selecting a row.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
FindCandidateByProposal

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
FindCandidateByProposalResult

#### getCandidateWork

##### DESCRIPTION

Reads the accessible native Candidate, revision, target, history and effective review state.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
CandidateWorkSelection

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
CandidateWorkResult

#### editCandidateWork

##### DESCRIPTION

Applies an explicit human work command using the observed native Entity revision; retains exact source and attributed decision history.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
CandidateWorkEdit

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
CandidateWorkResult

#### decideCandidateWork

##### DESCRIPTION

Applies an explicit human work command using the observed native Entity revision; retains exact source and attributed decision history.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
CandidateWorkDecision

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
CandidateWorkResult

#### admitCandidateWork

##### SUMMARY

Admit approved Information.

##### DESCRIPTION

Submits the exact current human-approved target to KnowledgeHub once, after native persistence of its Information identity. Existing uncertain submissions require lookup, never automatic resend.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
AdmitCandidateWork

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
CandidateWorkResult

#### confirmCandidateAdmission

##### SUMMARY

Confirm Information Admission.

##### DESCRIPTION

Reads only the reserved Information identity from KnowledgeHub, compares the complete original approved target and trace, and retains a confirmed native outcome without resubmitting.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
ConfirmCandidateAdmission

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
CandidateWorkResult

#### listCandidates

##### DESCRIPTION

Returns accessible InformationCandidates as items. Optional text matches a
case-insensitive substring of name or description; without text, all accessible
rows are eligible. Optional offset and limit apply through native query paging.
This query does not create candidates.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
ListCandidates

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
ListCandidatesResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-search

##### ENTITY
InformationCandidate

# SERVICE

## MaterialWork

### DESCRIPTION

Supports Material search, metadata inspection and original preview before Candidate
creation. Dispatch uses the public KnowledgeLake/Material Operations through normal
CNCF caller execution, security and observability context. TKL owns Material identity
and the logical wire schema; these consumer bindings do not define another Material
index or provider model. Reads never access Drive or private TKL implementation APIs,
mutate Candidates, or require or start OpenClaw processing. Local preview is not a
persisted evidence selection; explicit createCandidateFromMaterial retains the
selected source through native Candidate proposal registration.
Structured upstream failures remain unchanged without privileged fallback. Existing
reads remain read-only; separate explicit neutral registration work requests target
the fixed public KnowledgeLake/Material producer. TKL owns registration identity,
status, authorization, managed custody and physical effects. These declarations do
not establish implementation availability or expose a credential or general proxy
operation.

### OPERATION

#### createCandidateFromMaterial

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### DESCRIPTION

Explicitly create Candidate work from an exact caller-authorized Material/resource
selection under docs/spec/material-candidate-work-v1.md. Validate local input first,
look up the exact workbench-material/proposalId intent with the same caller, and
return current work on resend without source reads or overwriting human edits.
For absent intent inspect public logical metadata, retain the first selection in
originalProposal and register an unprepared proposal with unverified evidence.
No source revision/snapshot is inferred. Native Candidate persistence and acknowledged
identity remain authoritative; failures and unknown outcomes are never replayed.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### CreateCandidateFromMaterial

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------|------|--------------|
| proposalId | string | 1 |
| materialRef | string | 1 |
| resourceIds | string | * |
| name | name | 1 |
| content | string | 1 |
| context | string | ? |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RegisterProposalResult

#### refreshCandidateMaterialEvidence

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### DESCRIPTION

Explicitly acquire and apply caller-authorized TKL evidence for the immutable first
Material/resource selection. Validate native revision, reason and binding ownership
before source access. Preserve human target and history; effective changes require
new Review/Approve. Identical observations retain state and revision after a fresh
native revision check. Detached human references conflict without source access.
Use getCandidateWork to reconcile uncertain acknowledgements; never replay writes.

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RefreshCandidateMaterialEvidence

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

CandidateWorkResult

#### searchMaterials

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### DESCRIPTION

Dispatch to public KnowledgeLake/Material/searchMaterials with the caller's context.
Use case-insensitive title/reference substring search with text at most 256
characters. Offset defaults to 0 and must be nonnegative; limit defaults to 20 and
must be between 1 and 100. Authorization precedes stable reference ordering and
paging, including hasMore, without disclosing unauthorized metadata. Empty results
contain an empty items collection. Searching does not persist an evidence selection.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialSearchQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name   | type   | multiplicity |
|--------|--------|--------------|
| text   | string | ?            |
| offset | int    | ?            |
| limit  | int    | ?            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialSearchResult

#### inspectMaterial

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### DESCRIPTION

Dispatch to public KnowledgeLake/Material/getMaterial with the caller's context.
Pass the opaque TKL-issued materialRef unchanged. Caller admission and Material
read authorization precede resource access. Return the producer's logical metadata,
resources and attributed provenance unchanged without physical provider details.
Inspection is local preview and does not persist a Candidate evidence association.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialSelectionQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name        | type   | multiplicity |
|-------------|--------|--------------|
| materialRef | string | 1            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialMetadata

#### readOriginal

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### DESCRIPTION

Dispatch to public KnowledgeLake/Material/readOriginal with the caller's context,
passing the opaque materialRef and logical resourceId unchanged. Caller
authentication, Operation admission and Material/resource read authorization remain
with the public producer route. Preserve the admitted original bytes, media type,
private/no-store, nosniff, sandbox and attachment headers unchanged, without another
byte store or resource substitution on failure. Reading provides local preview;
it does not persist an evidence selection or start preparation or registration.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### OriginalSelectionQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name        | type   | multiplicity |
|-------------|--------|--------------|
| materialRef | string | 1            |
| resourceId  | string | 1            |

##### OUTPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialOriginalResult

######## EXTENDS

OperationResult

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name    | type | multiplicity |
|---------|------|--------------|
| content | blob | 1            |

#### createMaterialRegistration

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### DESCRIPTION

Forward one complete textus.material-contribution/1 contribution JSON unchanged to
org.simplemodeling.textus.KnowledgeLake/Material/createMaterialRegistration through
the same caller's CNCF execution, security and observability context. Preserve opaque
documents, source references, histories and Unicode; Studio owns authorized source
conversion and TKL alone interprets provider receipts. No Book, owner, location,
connection or target selector is added. TKL independently admits producer mode,
configuration, subject and native create authorization, then acknowledges Prepared
only after durable native creation without provider IO. Preserve OperationResponse,
registrationId, positive native revision, state and planned materialRef unchanged;
default result JSON retains registration_id/material_ref. Only registered is
available to normal reads. Native admission/storage/uncertainty Conclusions remain
unchanged. Unknown creation stays unresolved: no automatic retry, App-key dedupe,
grant copying, privileged fallback or Candidate mutation. This is a declaration
pending normal generation and fixed-forward implementation.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialRegistrationCreateCommand

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name         | type | multiplicity |
|--------------|------|--------------|
| contribution | json | 1            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialRegistrationResult

#### getMaterialRegistration

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### DESCRIPTION

Forward the exact opaque native registrationId to
org.simplemodeling.textus.KnowledgeLake/Material/getMaterialRegistration through the
same caller's CNCF execution, security and observability context. Never normalize
or derive the ID from a Material URN, provider or App/business key. TKL independently
applies producer mode, actual caller admission and native read authorization.
Preserve its OperationResponse, registrationId, positive committed native revision,
actual prepared/materializing/registered state and planned materialRef unchanged;
default result JSON retains registration_id/material_ref. A planned reference is
unavailable until registered. Missing/unauthorized records and native load failures
retain their exact Conclusions. Status reads perform no write, credential/provider
access, Candidate mutation or replay and authorize no retry, reset or deletion.
No polling, resume or bulk parameter is accepted. This declaration alone does not
establish generated or runtime availability.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialRegistrationSelectionQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name           | type   | multiplicity |
|----------------|--------|--------------|
| registrationId | string | 1            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialRegistrationResult

#### materializeMaterial

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### DESCRIPTION

Forward only the exact opaque native registrationId to
org.simplemodeling.textus.KnowledgeLake/Material/materializeMaterial through the
same caller's CNCF execution, security and observability context. TKL independently
owns producer mode/configuration/subject, native read/write and managed custody
authorization, retained destination admission and physical source/writer execution.
Its acknowledged durable Materializing transition must precede physical effects;
only confirmed native persistence returns Registered. Preserve OperationResponse,
registrationId, positive committed native revision, actual state and materialRef
unchanged, including native default registration_id/material_ref result JSON.
Only registered enables ordinary search/get/read. Exact native authorization,
state-conflict, provider and uncertain-acknowledgement Conclusions remain unchanged.
Failure can retain Materializing and bytes, or unknown final acknowledgement can
leave Registered; explicit getMaterialRegistration reads actual status without
authorizing replay. Never automatically retry/reset/delete, add a write, substitute
direct provider access or a privileged identity, or mutate a Candidate. This
declaration does not establish generated or runtime implementation availability.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialRegistrationMaterializeCommand

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name           | type   | multiplicity |
|----------------|--------|--------------|
| registrationId | string | 1            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialRegistrationResult

